                    <h1 class="font-display text-[34px] leading-[1.12] font-extrabold tracking-[-0.02em] text-balance md:text-[42px] ">Supercharge Your Habit Tracking with HabitKit and iOS Shortcuts</h1>
                    <p class="text-[17px] leading-[1.65] text-muted text-pretty">Discover how to connect HabitKit with iOS Shortcuts to automate habit completion and reduce manual tracking friction.</p>

            <img
            src="https://habitkit.app/blog-assets/title/shortcuts.webp"
            alt="HabitKit Automations in the Shortcuts app"
            width="1600"
            height="900"
            class="mt-2 w-full rounded-[18px] border border-white/8"
        >
    
    <div class="text-[15px] leading-[1.75] text-muted [&amp;_ul]:list-disc [&amp;_ul]:pl-5 [&amp;_strong]:font-semibold [&amp;_strong]:text-foam [&amp;_a]:text-accent-soft [&amp;_a]:transition-colors [&amp;_a:hover]:text-accent text-[15.5px] [&amp;&gt;*+*]:mt-4 [&amp;_ul]:space-y-2 [&amp;_ol]:list-decimal [&amp;_ol]:space-y-2 [&amp;_ol]:pl-5 [&amp;_h2]:mt-9 [&amp;_h2]:font-display [&amp;_h2]:text-[23px] [&amp;_h2]:font-bold [&amp;_h2]:text-foam [&amp;_h3]:mt-7 [&amp;_h3]:font-display [&amp;_h3]:text-[18px] [&amp;_h3]:font-bold [&amp;_h3]:text-foam [&amp;_img]:mx-auto [&amp;_img]:my-7 [&amp;_img]:max-h-[560px] [&amp;_img]:w-auto [&amp;_img]:max-w-full [&amp;_img]:rounded-[14px] [&amp;_img]:border [&amp;_img]:border-white/8 [&amp;_blockquote]:border-l-2 [&amp;_blockquote]:border-accent/40 [&amp;_blockquote]:pl-4 [&amp;_hr]:my-8 [&amp;_hr]:border-white/8 [&amp;_code]:rounded [&amp;_code]:bg-white/8 [&amp;_code]:px-1.5 [&amp;_code]:py-0.5 [&amp;_code]:font-mono [&amp;_code]:text-[13.5px] article-body mt-4">
    <p>Discover the secrets of integrating iOS Shortcuts with your favorite habit-tracking app to simplify your daily routines.</p>
<p>Imagine a workflow where habit tracking seamlessly integrates with your daily activities, automatically checking off goals as you move through the day. With HabitKit and iOS Shortcuts, that workflow is possible today.</p>
<p>By connecting HabitKit habits to iOS automations, you can build a reliable system that works behind the scenes to keep you consistent.</p>
<h2>Download HabitKit</h2>
<ul>
<li><a href="https://apps.apple.com/us/app/habit-tracker-habitkit/id6443918070">Download on iOS</a></li>
<li><a href="https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=com.roehl.habitkit">Download on Google Play</a></li>
</ul>
<p>This setup saves time and mental energy while improving tracking accuracy. Instead of remembering to log habits manually, your phone can trigger completions based on workouts, locations, or time of day.</p>
<h2>Setup Guide: Connecting HabitKit to iOS Shortcuts</h2>
<ol>
<li>Install <strong>Shortcuts</strong> from the <a href="https://apps.apple.com/us/app/shortcuts/id915249334">App Store</a>.</li>
<li>Make sure your habits are already created in HabitKit.</li>
<li>Set up your automation trigger:
<ul>
<li>Tap <strong>Automation</strong> at the bottom of the Shortcuts app.</li>
<li>Tap the <strong>+</strong> button to create a new automation.</li>
<li>Choose a trigger, for example <strong>When I start a workout</strong>.</li>
<li>Configure trigger details, for example <strong>Workout Type: Running</strong>, trigger type <strong>Ends</strong>, and optionally <strong>Run Immediately</strong>.</li>
<li>Tap <strong>Next</strong> and choose <strong>New Blank Automation</strong>.</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ol>
<p><img src="/blog-assets/ios-shortcuts-habit-tracker-00.webp" alt="Open Shortcuts automation tab" />
<img src="/blog-assets/ios-shortcuts-habit-tracker-01.webp" alt="Create a new automation in Shortcuts" />
<img src="/blog-assets/ios-shortcuts-habit-tracker-02.webp" alt="Select a trigger event in Shortcuts" />
<img src="/blog-assets/ios-shortcuts-habit-tracker-03.webp" alt="Configure workout trigger details" /></p>
<ol start="4">
<li>Tap <strong>Add Action</strong>.</li>
<li>Scroll to HabitKit and choose <strong>Complete Habit</strong>.</li>
<li>Expand the blue caret menu and select the habit in the <strong>Habit</strong> field.</li>
<li>Tap <strong>Done</strong> to finish your first HabitKit automation.</li>
</ol>
<p><img src="/blog-assets/ios-shortcuts-habit-tracker-04.webp" alt="Add action in Shortcuts automation" />
